# Guides for scales: guides

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:giggly, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"}
  ])
```

## About this notebook

This notebook follows the examples on ggplot2's reference page for
[`guides()`](https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/guides.html), in the order the page gives
them. Each example shows ggplot2's code first and then Giggly's. An example Giggly cannot draw yet
keeps its ggplot2 code and names what it is waiting for, so the page is also a list of what
remains.

Every scale is read back through a guide: an axis for a position scale, a legend or a colour bar for
the others. Each scale's `guide` argument sets its guide; `guides()` sets them all at once, by
aesthetic, each as a guide's name, such as `"legend"`, or a call to a guide function. A guide set to
`"none"` is left out, and legends that show the same values under the same title merge into one.
Giggly has none of it yet, but reads each scale back as ggplot2 does by default: `x` and `y` with
axes, `alpha` and a discrete `colour` or `fill` with a legend, and a continuous `colour` or `fill`
with a colour bar.

## The guides ggplot2 chooses

`p` maps `colour` to a continuous column and `size` and `shape` to discrete ones (`factor()` makes
a column discrete), so ggplot2 reads `colour` back with a colour bar and the others with legends.

```r
# ggplot object

dat <- data.frame(x = 1:5, y = 1:5, p = 1:5, q = factor(1:5),
 r = factor(1:5))
p <-
  ggplot(dat, aes(x, y, colour = p, size = q, shape = r)) +
  geom_point()

# without guide specification
p
```

Not in Giggly yet: mapping `size` and `shape`, the scales that map them and the legends that read
them back.

## Choosing each guide

```r
# Show colorbar guide for colour.
# All these examples below have a same effect.

p + guides(colour = "colorbar", size = "legend", shape = "legend")
p + guides(colour = guide_colorbar(), size = guide_legend(),
  shape = guide_legend())
p +
 scale_colour_continuous(guide = "colorbar") +
 scale_size_discrete(guide = "legend") +
 scale_shape(guide = "legend")
```

Not in Giggly yet: mapping `size` and `shape`, `guide_colourbar()`, `scale_size_discrete()` and
`scale_shape()`.

## Removing guides

```r
 # Remove some guides
 p + guides(colour = "none")
 p + guides(colour = "colorbar",size = "none")
```

Not in Giggly yet: mapping `size` and `shape` and the legends that read them back.

## Merged legends

Legends with the same title that show the same values merge into one, each key showing a colour,
a size and a shape together.

```r
# Guides are integrated where possible

p +
  guides(
    colour = guide_legend("title"),
    size = guide_legend("title"),
    shape = guide_legend("title")
 )
# same as
g <- guide_legend("title")
p + guides(colour = g, size = g, shape = g)
```

Not in Giggly yet: mapping `size` and `shape`, and `guide_legend()`'s `title` option.

## Legends below the plot

```r
p + theme(legend.position = "bottom")
```

Not in Giggly yet: mapping `size` and `shape` and the legends that read them back, and changing the
theme, here to put the legends below the plot.

## The order of the legends

```r
# position of guides

# Set order for multiple guides
ggplot(mpg, aes(displ, cty)) +
  geom_point(aes(size = hwy, colour = cyl, shape = drv)) +
  guides(
   colour = guide_colourbar(order = 1),
   shape = guide_legend(order = 2),
   size = guide_legend(order = 3)
 )
```

Not in Giggly yet: mapping `size` and `shape`, `guide_colourbar()`, and the `order` option of
`guide_colourbar()` and `guide_legend()`, which sets the order the guides are drawn in.